 Text: eSchool Administrator Financial File: It handles student enrollment, exam scheduling, and financial transactions, including discounts and fees, with documents automatically sent to the accounting department. Transfers are managed through registration, using the eSchool Driver and Safety app for monitoring. Clubs are defined and students enrolled, generating specific lists. The cafeteria issues cards linked to balances for purchases, directly connected to accounting. Financial reports enable analysis of revenue, installments, and overdue payments, with reminders sent to parents via the eSchool Connect app. It deals with defining financial accounts and cost centers, linking payment vouchers and daily entries to these centers to obtain profit and loss results for each center. The school can control its expenses through various program settings linked to the budget. It includes several accounting statements that can be extracted from the trial balance, account statement, accounts receivable statement, cash flow statement, etc. Assets management allows for the preparation of asset purchase invoices and their automatic transfer to accounting, tracking maintenance for each asset to monitor its consumption and transfer its book value at the end of the financial cycle to accounting. Mechanisms management involves entering all information related to the school's machinery, daily maintenance, and recording incidents, with multiple reports extracted accordingly. It is responsible for defining the school's warehouses, including defining items and linking them to categories so that users can generate sales invoices or point of sale transactions, enter purchase invoices, and delivery and receipt orders within the school departments, which are then directly transferred to the accounting department. Additionally, various reports are available, such as item movement statements, profit and loss statements at the item level, inventory lists, item sales by cost centers, and more. It manages routes, vehicles, and student assignments for efficient commuting. It includes features like route definition, vehicle details, student allocation, real-time tracking, and communication for updates and safety measures, enhancing transportation logistics for the school community.
